WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.900 line:88%
Assessment answers three questions.

00:00:02.655 --> 00:00:03.850 line:88%
Is intervention needed?

00:00:04.665 --> 00:00:05.760 line:88%
What should the goals be?

00:00:06.655 --> 00:00:07.650 line:88%
Is intervention working?

00:00:08.555 --> 00:00:11.240 line:88%
Combine a formal measure with a spontaneous or structured

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.140 line:88%
language sample.

00:00:13.095 --> 00:00:17.340 line:88%
The sample shows how vocabulary, sentence structure, and communication

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.160 line:88%
work together in play or a story.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.460 line:88%
The lecture describes the Rossetti as a criterion referenced

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.520 line:88%
developmental scale.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.760 line:88%
A developmental checklist and a comparison with a standardized

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.140 line:88%
normative sample answer different questions.

00:00:33.473 --> 00:00:37.473 line:88%
Before testing, check the child's technology, reduce noise and

00:00:37.473 --> 00:00:40.593 line:88%
distractions, and consider the primary communication mode.

00:00:41.498 --> 00:00:45.493 line:88%
Keep standardized administration and scoring separate from additional probing.

00:00:46.313 --> 00:00:48.713 line:88%
Suppose a child misses an item under the required

00:00:48.713 --> 00:00:51.393 line:88%
procedure, then succeeds after an extra gesture.

00:00:52.193 --> 00:00:53.993 line:88%
Preserve the standardized response.

00:00:54.643 --> 00:00:58.183 line:88%
Record the supported response as qualitative information about access

00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:58.943 line:88%
and learning.

00:00:59.743 --> 00:01:01.863 line:88%
It can help plan therapy, but it does not

00:01:01.863 --> 00:01:04.473 line:88%
become credit on the original standardized item.

00:01:05.273 --> 00:01:07.883 line:88%
A test score must be interpreted with its procedures,

00:01:08.223 --> 00:01:10.103 line:88%
norms, and communication demands.
